findings.body:
The hunk was meant to fix `set_cookie`, but it changes the `WebviewMessage` in `delete_cookie`. In the base, `set_cookie` already sends `SetCookie` (line 1706 in head), and `delete_cookie` sends `DeleteCookie`. After this PR, `delete_cookie` (lines 1712-1722) sends `SetCookie`, so calling `window.delete_cookie(c)` sets the cookie in the webview instead of removing it. Nothing in the diff adds a test that would catch this.

::diff{file="crates/tauri-runtime-wry/src/lib.rs" lines="1712-1722"}

::callout{type="warning"}
The `.clone()` removal is correct on its own, since `cookie` is taken by value. The fix is to keep `DeleteCookie` and only drop the clone.

::suggestion{file="crates/tauri-runtime-wry/src/lib.rs" lines="1718"}
WebviewMessage::DeleteCookie(cookie.into_owned()),

The PR description covers three items, but the diff also renames the public builder method `WebviewWindowBuilder::with_window_features` to `window_features`. The doc example and the `on_new_window` call sites are updated to match. The method is part of the unreleased `on_new_window` feature (`.changes/on_new_window.md`), so this is probably not breaking for a released version. But the rename is unannounced and the changelog does not mention it. The `with_` prefix also matches neighbouring builder methods such as `with_webview_configuration`, so the rename makes the API less consistent.

::diff{file="crates/tauri/src/webview/webview_window.rs" lines="1304-1322"}

::callout{type="info"}
If the rename is intentional, document it in the PR and the changefile. If not, revert it to `with_window_features`.

The new `inner_size` and `position` calls have irregular spacing (`size.width,    size.height` and `position.x,position.y`). `cargo fmt --check` will fail, and Tauri's CI runs that check. The same lines were correctly formatted in the base.

::diff{file="crates/tauri/src/webview/webview_window.rs" lines="1315-1322"}

::suggestion{file="crates/tauri/src/webview/webview_window.rs" lines="1317-1321"}
    if let Some(size) = features.size() {
      self.window_builder = self.window_builder.inner_size(size.width, size.height);
    }

    if let Some(position) = features.position() {
      self.window_builder = self.window_builder.position(position.x, position.y);
    }

The base applied `position` before `inner_size`. The PR swaps the order without explanation and without touching the logic. For a tao `WindowBuilder`, both are builder attributes applied at build time, so the order probably has no effect. The swap is still unrelated churn in a PR described as a regression fix, and it makes the diff harder to review.

::diff{file="crates/tauri/src/webview/webview_window.rs" lines="1316-1322"}

If the order was not intentional, restore the base order to keep the diff focused.
